00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:48.863
In upcoming videos,
we'll get hands-on

00:00:48.863 --> 00:00:50.530
and I'll show you how
to wrap management

00:00:50.530 --> 00:00:52.900
around your APIs in minutes.

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:56.260
Before we do that,
let's cover some basics.

00:00:56.260 --> 00:01:00.160
The key concept enabling the API
management goodness in Apigee

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:02.450
Edge is the API proxy.

00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:05.110
A proxy is a wrapper
for your actual service.

00:01:05.110 --> 00:01:08.200
Clients, instead of calling
your API endpoint directly,

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:12.610
call the API proxy, and the API
proxy calls your existing API.

00:01:12.610 --> 00:01:14.830
You may be thinking,
why the extra hop?

00:01:14.830 --> 00:01:17.170
Why use one extra moving part?

00:01:17.170 --> 00:01:18.220
Well, I'll tell you.

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:20.410
The API proxy provides
the way to plug

00:01:20.410 --> 00:01:23.650
in an application-independent
mechanism for you

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:27.040
to specify consistent management
rules and policies that

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:29.320
apply to all of your APIs.

00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:31.330
Your APIs might be
a mix of services,

00:01:31.330 --> 00:01:35.110
lacking consistency with respect
to security, or data model,

00:01:35.110 --> 00:01:38.260
or even URL design,
and an API proxy

00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:40.360
allows you to build
a coherent facade

00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:42.790
around those various endpoints.

00:01:42.790 --> 00:01:46.840
Or maybe all of your APIs are
clean, new implementations,

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:50.170
so you don't need a proxy
to enforce consistency,

00:01:50.170 --> 00:01:52.930
but you will still want an
API proxy to handle things

00:01:52.930 --> 00:01:56.980
like OAuth token verification
or caching, routing,

00:01:56.980 --> 00:02:00.540
rate limiting, and
analytics and reporting.

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:03.180
Apigee can provide all
of that with no coding

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:06.550
and no modification of
your existing services.

00:02:06.550 --> 00:02:08.250
So that's API management.

00:02:08.250 --> 00:02:12.240
Apigee Edge lets you easily
add management to any API.

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:13.560
Ready to get started?

